From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:47:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: build and test the pack on every change, and once a day

Adds `.github/workflows/build.yml`. On a push to main, a pull request, a
daily schedule and on demand, it installs, then runs `npm test` (which
builds the components, runs the comment gate and the dependency gate,
and then the suite), the comment gate's own tests, and sdkgen's package
check.

Two lanes: the dependencies a consumer resolves today, and the floor
`peerDependencies` declares, read from the manifest. The schedule is
there because the dependency is the published sdkgen: a release that
breaks a target is not a push here.

AGENTS.md and COMMENT-POLICY.md said that no CI runs yet. They now say
what runs.

Checked before it was written out as a patch: actionlint 1.7.12 with
shellcheck 0.9.0 over the workflow, clean. Each step's commands were
run by hand on Node 22.23.4, in both lanes, and pass; the floor lane's
script pinned sdkgen 4.44.0 and apidef 8.25.0. The suite also passes on
Node 24.22.3, the version the workflow sets up. The workflow itself has
not run: a session cannot push one.

